WEBVTT

00:00:00.064 --> 00:00:14.456
Welcome! In this walkthrough, we follow James, a patient from the United States, through every screen of the Heal India Global patient experience. Part one covers the website, the dashboard and the AI screening.

00:00:18.768 --> 00:00:28.120
It all starts on the public website. Patients see the promise up front: world-class treatment in India, at a fraction of the cost back home.

00:00:28.437 --> 00:00:36.205
They can browse specialties, real cost examples, and accredited partner hospitals, before they ever create an account.

00:00:39.232 --> 00:00:48.464
Patients, agents and hospitals all use one secure sign-in door. James types his email and password, and lands in his own portal.

00:00:50.303 --> 00:00:59.175
This is the patient dashboard. It counts down to the next admission, and shows the booking, the hospital and the doctor at a glance.

00:00:59.486 --> 00:01:07.974
Below, a pre-travel checklist, quick actions, today's schedule and recent AI screenings keep the whole journey in one place.

00:01:08.282 --> 00:01:14.298
The header holds the notification bell, a light and dark theme switch, and the account menu.

00:01:19.896 --> 00:01:29.224
Under Care, AI screenings lists every assessment James has started. Tabs separate the ones with matches ready from the ones not finished yet.

00:01:32.026 --> 00:01:40.826
Starting a new AI screening begins with one simple question: what brings you to India? Each specialty shows the typical savings.

00:01:46.092 --> 00:01:55.540
Step one is an interactive body map. James marks where the problem is, or picks an area from the list, and can even describe it by voice.

00:01:57.973 --> 00:02:05.837
Step two asks about symptoms, with quick yes, maybe, or no answers, and room to add anything that is missing.

00:02:09.166 --> 00:02:18.614
Step three covers how long the condition has lasted, how severe it is, and any previous treatment. Reports can be attached right here.

00:02:21.064 --> 00:02:32.360
Finally, James personalizes his matches by language, doctor gender, budget and travel window. His answers are saved as a draft, so he can come back anytime.

00:02:35.149 --> 00:02:44.933
When a screening is complete, the AI explains the findings in plain language: a summary, possible conditions to discuss, and suggested specialties.

00:02:45.243 --> 00:02:56.635
It then lists matched doctors and hospitals, with filters for city, accreditation, price and rating. Each match can be saved, compared, or asked for a quote.

00:02:56.952 --> 00:03:04.912
A treatment cost comparison shows what the same procedure costs in India versus at home, which is often the deciding factor.

00:03:05.224 --> 00:03:14.096
Selecting two or three matches opens a side by side comparison of doctors, hospitals, experience, inclusions and price.

00:03:14.529 --> 00:03:22.609
That is part one. In part two, James follows his quotes, books and pays for treatment, and plans his trip.

00:03:24.144 --> 00:03:35.440
Welcome back! Part two follows James from his quotes to the trip home: cases, bookings and payments, the trip hub, documents, messages and his profile.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:47.136
Every quote request becomes a case. My cases shows them all, with status tabs from waiting for a quote, to booked, to completed.

00:03:47.775 --> 00:03:54.271
Filters and search make it easy to find a case, for example only the ones where a quote has arrived.

00:03:54.605 --> 00:04:05.277
Inside a case, James sees the hospital's itemized quote, and can accept or decline it. Documents, details and a full timeline sit on the same page.

00:04:05.684 --> 00:04:12.612
From a quote, James can go straight to booking: he picks the admission date and confirms who is traveling with him.

00:04:16.692 --> 00:04:26.020
Bookings lists every confirmed treatment, with tabs for awaiting payment, confirmed, admitted and completed, and a filter for anything left to pay.

00:04:26.339 --> 00:04:32.235
A booking shows the treatment, the payment schedule with receipts, and a clear price summary.

00:04:35.242 --> 00:04:44.450
Paying is secure and simple. James sees exactly what is due, and chooses a payment method, card or international bank transfer.

00:04:46.364 --> 00:04:53.388
Payments and receipts collects every transaction in one place, with status tabs and downloadable receipts.

00:04:57.189 --> 00:05:07.453
The trip hub is James's travel companion: a pre-arrival checklist, visa support, flights and transfers, accommodation, and a translator or local guide.

00:05:07.773 --> 00:05:16.021
It also has the itinerary, 24/7 help numbers, cultural tips for India, and an SOS button for emergencies.

00:05:18.788 --> 00:05:26.964
Documents keeps medical reports, scans and the passport together. Files can be uploaded and filtered by type.

00:05:27.282 --> 00:05:36.106
And with AI report reading, James can upload or photograph a medical report, and get a plain-language summary that he confirms before it is shared.

00:05:41.134 --> 00:05:47.678
Messages connects James with hospitals and his care coordinator, with one conversation per case.

00:05:48.004 --> 00:05:55.844
He can also contact support at any time. Here he asks his coordinator a quick question about the airport pickup.

00:05:59.566 --> 00:06:07.790
Notifications collect every update, from new quotes to payment confirmations, with an unread filter and mark all as read.

00:06:11.759 --> 00:06:17.703
Saved keeps the hospitals, doctors and procedures James bookmarked while researching.

00:06:20.091 --> 00:06:27.763
In the profile, James manages his personal information and home address, along with medical and insurance details.

00:06:28.084 --> 00:06:35.948
Separate tabs hold the passport and emergency contact, travel companions, and language and notification preferences.

00:06:37.559 --> 00:06:46.671
Privacy and account shows every consent with its date, and lets him request account deletion. Security handles his password and sessions.

00:06:46.979 --> 00:06:53.667
Finally, the sidebar can be collapsed to icons for more room, and expanded again with one click.

00:06:53.982 --> 00:07:01.198
That is the complete patient journey, from the first AI screening to the trip home. Thank you for watching!
